  "verbalization": "Seco-plakortolide K appears to interact with Peptide deformylase through a shared target of 8-Pentadecanone, which is implicated in multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that seco-plakortolide K may act as a modulator of 8-Pentadecanone, which in turn targets Peptide deformylase. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple pathways where seco-plakortolide K is linked to 8-Pentadecanone, and both are ultimately directed toward Peptide deformylase. The mechanism is likely indirect, as 8-Pentadecanone is a common target across different pathways, suggesting a potential role in the regulation of Peptide deformylase. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible functional link between seco-plakortolide K and Peptide deformylase, mediated through 8-Pentadecanone.",
